website or web application.\u00a0It&#8217;s\u00a0the part\u00a0of the development process that handles the &#8220;behind-the-scenes&#8221; functionality, data management, and the server&#8217;s interaction with the client-side (front-end) of a website.\u00a0<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Backend developers manage the server where the website or web application is hosted. This includes setting up and configuring the server, ensuring its security, and&nbsp;optimizing&nbsp;its performance.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Backend developers design and&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;the database systems that store and manage the website&#8217;s data. This involves creating database schemas,&nbsp;optimizing&nbsp;database queries, and ensuring data integrity.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The developers also write code to handle server-side logic, which includes processing user requests, authentication, authorization, and business logic. They&nbsp;determine&nbsp;how data is retrieved and presented to the user.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What Are Backend Programming Languages?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Backend programming languages\u00a0are used to build and run\u00a0the server-side systems that power a web application. They handle everything users\u00a0don&#8217;t\u00a0see &#8211; processing requests, managing data, and enabling communication between the server and the client.\u00a0<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>If you want to become a backend developer, our web development course teaches you these&nbsp;backend languages for web development&nbsp;and the frameworks used to build:&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Websites\u00a0<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Interactive online tools\u00a0<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Mobile apps\u00a0<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Desktop apps\u00a0<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Web servers\u00a0<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Software prototypes\u00a0<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Online games\u00a0<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Security features\u00a0<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Data collection\u00a0<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Networking<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n    <!-- LOTTIE SCRIPT